WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.826
ToolSpace: Scaling Tool-Centric Environment Synthesis for Long-Horizon Agents. Renmin University of China and Fudan University.

00:00:05.089 --> 00:00:06.512
Beyond isolated environments.

00:00:06.619 --> 00:00:07.983
Connect real tools.

00:00:08.088 --> 00:00:09.150
Walk across worlds.

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:11.723
Google Sheets is an environment. Its tools read, find, update, append and clear values in persistent files and state.

00:00:11.723 --> 00:00:15.522
Follow the selected tool calls across environments; each hop updates the current tool and environment counts.

00:00:15.522 --> 00:00:17.667
A rejected candidate returns to its checkpoint. Resample and complete the walk.

00:00:17.667 --> 00:00:21.442
Expand into a wider ToolSpace of environments and connected tools.

00:00:21.442 --> 00:00:26.463
A successful tool chain becomes a natural-language task and assertion scripts: a goal without tool names or execution order; programmatic checks through environment APIs and state or output validation.

00:00:26.463 --> 00:00:32.702
Train from Qwen3-8B, Qwen3.6-35B-A3B and GLM-5.2. All use SFT; the 8B and 35B models continue with Agent RL. The 744B model uses SFT.

00:00:32.702 --> 00:00:38.585
ToolSpace-744B-A40B averages 56.6 over seven benchmarks, tied with Claude Opus 5 and above Kimi K3 and GPT 5.6 Sol.

00:00:38.585 --> 00:00:41.953
ToolSpace upgrades AutomationBench and Tau3 Banking into two harder Pro benchmarks.

00:00:41.953 --> 00:00:45.946
For both Pro benchmarks, each of seven models moves from its standard score to the updated Pro score. Grey bars retain the standard score; coloured bars shrink and the score drops appear.

00:00:45.946 --> 00:00:48.400
Updated Pro scores for seven frontier models include DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017: 22.3 on AutomationBench Pro and 36.9 on Tau3 Banking Pro.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.604
With the same Qwen3.6-35B-A3B backbone, more environment clusters improve performance.

00:00:52.604 --> 00:00:56.333
Increasing the training-data fraction also improves performance.

00:00:56.333 --> 00:00:58.434
Separate environment and data scaling experiments from paper Figure 7.

00:00:58.434 --> 00:01:00.000
ToolSpace. toolspace-agent.github.io
